rse’s eye UVs, add a safe Western Hotel yard viewpoint, and keep release-note text inside the Navigator.\n\n- T-3083: V18 rounds the upper lamp housings and narrows the lower bodies, preserving non-lamp geometry, materials, nodes, contacts, collision proxy and runtime policies. V17 remains archived.\n- T-3086: separately versioned d4544c28 reproduces from canonical b479 with the declared eye UV correction. Geometry, rig, weights, animation, materials and all six embedded images are preserved.\n- T-3087: adds E−124/N−292/yaw221.19. All 19 viewpoints are dry and outside roofs; the previous 18 and actor placement are unchanged.\n- T-3125: three news grids gain a zero-minimum flexible column and long-text wrapping. No font reduction or clipping mask. Exactly one visitor item joins the existing T-3083 changelog anchor.\n\nThe original feature commits remain intact. The latest merge incorporates accepted DEV 70bcc436, including Glessner, First Presbyterian and the 1811 Prairie kit changes, while preserving the transport files and original ROADMAP bytes. Shared licence, liberties, STATUS and ROADMAP records describe the group. Broader photographic, native/world, gait, tack, team, occupant and riding acceptance remains open with the existing remainder tickets; T-2794/T-2800 stay split.\n\nCurrent head: 1b70cdbd85b18c124870d6274d2ffffd4ca5979b; tree 9fa9511eabff9a0e42da32410edf09a8e3608889; app subtree da9f71f6749ebf52e09ad51f673a9e4debbf4478.\n\nValidation:\n\n- Full preflight passed 1,066 steps / 384 self-tests in 645.208s against explicit pinned BASE 70bcc436. Actual return code 0; 721 descendants reaped, none remaining. The committed tree exactly equals the validated tree. Canonical liberties/source-use/jaunt checks passed with all 752 liberties. Exact committed-HEAD changelog and ID questions passed. Actual committed-head publication passed in44.673s with complete cleanup.\n- Fresh focused news checks at both widths and normal/140% text size, all 15 browser parts at both widths, and fresh ordinary CI must complete before DEV delivery.\n- Earlier H330 focused checks passed97 assertions at both widths and normal/140% text sizes in1200.667s, with final source/index/full-mirror bindings, zero errors and cleanup0. They remain tied to H330/notes2259, not this changed source. Earlier C4B8 focused checks passed 92 assertions. Its seven complete mobile legs covered parts 1–13, but that run was deliberately retired with outer code 130 and complete cleanup before the changed app was merged. Those results remain historical and are not counted on this head. Interrupted attempts, timeouts and the older 150-minute CI cancellation remain nonpasses.\n\nNo production promotion is claimed; merging stages to DEV only.\n\nSaved evidence: https://github.com/kevinrhaas/chicago-evidence/tree/f4c6beec5840eca95bb7c261e80383a0738f07b0/evidence/transport-recovery-2026-10-24/CHECKPOINT-32-H330-FOCUSED-PASS-AND-70B-INTAKE\n\n\n\n## Steward lap, 2026-10-25 (slice 5/5)\n\n- Merged `dev` in twice (34 commits, then T-3146 #1307). One conflict, `docs/STATUS.md` heads: kept both dev's T-3123 section and this PR's T-3083/T-3086/T-3087 section; nothing else conflicted.\n- `./tools/check.sh` on the first lap's tree: **CHECK PASS, 1069 steps, none red** (384 self-tests). The second dev lap brought only T-3146's Glessner budget files (`main.js`, its QA tool and receipts), none of which this PR touches. The hosted gate checks the head.\n- `check-changelog-entry.mjs` against the merge base: entry present (`changelog.d/T-3083.json`). `changelog-entries.mjs --check` OK.\n- Smoke by parts (published mirror, loaded 4-CPU runner shared by five slices, load about 5):\n  - mobile part 1: **95 pass, 0 fail, zero page errors**, exit 0\n  - desktop part 3 (citations, liberties): **107 pass, 0 fail, zero page errors**, exit 0\n  - desktop part 1: **65 pass, zero page errors**, then killed at the 585 s foreground cap. Its one FAIL line is that kill (\"Target page … has been closed\"), the same thing #1309 recorded on this runner. Dev's record has this leg passing in 7m13s.\n- Did not run: the other parts of the 15 that `--for-diff` names (the lane caps a run at four legs), and the focused 140%-text news check.\n","labels":[{"id":12374546158,"node_id":"LA_kwDOUoK9js8AAAAC4ZSW7g","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/kevinrhaas/chicago/labels/resume","name":"resume","description":"A run could not finish this; the next one picks it up — reason in the resume: comment","color":"0E8A16","default":false,"archived_at":null,"archived_by":null}],"milestone":null,"active_lock_reason":null,"created_at":"2026-10-24T10:26:08Z","updated_at":"2026-10-25T15:41:24Z","closed_at":"2026-10-25T15:41:24Z","merged_at":"2026-10-25T15:41:24Z","merge_commit_sha":"e03404d2cc275acfa06316835e088a1892289ab8","assignee":null,"assignees":[],"requested_reviewers":[],"requested_teams":[],"head":{"label":"kevinrhaas:steward/t3083-t3086-t3087-transport-recovery-20261024","ref":"steward/t3083-t3086-t3087-transport-recovery-20261024","repo":{"id":1384299918,"node_id":"R_kgDOUoK9jg","name":"chicago","full_name":"kevinrhaas/chicago","owner":{"login":"kevinrhaas","id":4193586,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjQxOTM1ODY=","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/4193586?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/kevinrhaas","html_url":"https://github.com/kevinrhaas","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/kevinrhaas/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/kevinrhaas/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/kevinrhaas/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/kevinrhaas/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/kevinrhaas/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/kevinrhaas/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/kevinrhaas/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/kevinrhaas/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/u